     Let $X = X(\pi,\sigma)$ be a Kato manifold with Kato modification
   $\pi : \widehat{\mathbb{B}} \to \mathbb{B}$. Let $\widehat{H}$ be the modification of a primary Hopf manifold $H$ obtained via small deformation from $X$. Then $\widehat{H}$ and $X$ have the same Hodge and Betti numbers.
