   Let $X = X(\pi,\sigma)$ be a Kato manifold with Kato modification 
$\pi : \widehat{\mathbb{B}} \to \mathbb{B}$. 
Then the Hodge numbers of $X$ are given by:
\[
h^{p,q}(X)=
\begin{cases}
1, & (p,q)\in\{(0,0),(0,1),(n,n-1),(n,n)\}\\
h^{p,q}(\widehat{\mathbb{CP}^n}) - h^{p,q}(\mathbb{CP}^n), &\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
\]
Moreover, the Betti numbers of $X$ satisfy:
\[
b_k(X)=
\begin{cases}
